        "type": "social_post",
        "content": "id: \"116967892835165166\"\nplatform: mastodon\npage: Mastodon@mastodon.social\ntitle: \"@Mastodon: It's time for our first Server Spotlight! We want to help people find their comm\"\nbody: \"It's time for our first Server Spotlight!\\nWe want to help people find their communities across the #fediverse so we're featuring servers here on this account.\\nFirst up: The Mended Drum, a home for fans of all things Sir Terry Pratchett.\\nIt is said that if you stay on The Mended Drum long enough, you'll meet every hero on the server: https://mendeddrum.org/directory\\n(keep an eye on your horse, though 😉)\\n#FeaturedServer #CommunitySpotlight #Mastodon #SocialWeb #GNUTerryPratchett\"\nauthor: Mastodon\nauthor_display_name: Mastodon\nauthor_avatar_url: \"https://files.mastodon.social/accounts/avatars/000/013/179/original/b4ceb19c9c54ec7e.png\"\nurl: \"https://mastodon.social/@Mastodon/116967892835165166\"\npublished_at: \"2026-07-23T06:33:23.881Z\"\nreply_count: 6\nrepost_count: 135\nlike_count: 224\nmedia_url: null\nthumbnail_url: null\nexternal_url: \"https://mendeddrum.org/directory\"\nexternal_title: The Mended Drum\ncomments[5]{id,author,author_display_name,body,url,published_at,like_count,reply_count,repost_count}:\n  \"116968031737433394\",wjmaggos@liberal.city,william ⁂ maggos,\"@Mastodon\\nI don't get thinking of servers as a community, except to the degree something like the fans of a podcast start a server to talk to each other AND figure out the fedi. but communities are insular and that's the opposite of interoperability. and everybody will soon have friends off server that they feel like are part of their community.\\na server shares mod policy. in order to avoid centralization, when no other sensible division makes sense, let's separate servers by locality.\",\"https://liberal.city/@wjmaggos/116968031703510314\",\"2026-07-23T07:08:42.000Z\",4,3,1\n  \"116968511717198649\",feyter@mastodon.gamedev.place,Feyter,\"@wjmaggos @Mastodon in fact moderation by topic makes sense, because local law of the district the server is located is one thing... But there are also social norms and behavior in a community that only members of that community can really understand. It's more about culture than about locality.\\nHowever, the fediverse has become so interconnected, that this gets very blurry.\",\"https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@feyter/116968511685664959\",\"2026-07-23T09:10:46.000Z\",1,0,0\n  \"116969217752337043\",Tho99@mendeddrum.org,\"Thomas =:-)\",\"@wjmaggos\\nQuite a few old timers from alt.fan.pratchett and various cons & meets make the drum their home.\\nSimplifies quite a few things.\",\"https://mendeddrum.org/@Tho99/116969217656856589\",\"2026-07-23T12:10:19.000Z\",6,1,0\n  \"116969610251697436\",wjmaggos@liberal.city,william ⁂ maggos,\"@Tho99\\nthat's very cool but they could instead form a more closed group using lots of other tools, like #matrix. still uses FOSS decentralized tech.\\nusing fedi for this brings up two problems imo.\\nfew people are part of one community. so you'd have to choose or have multiple personal accounts, something we're kinda trying to avoid.\\na norm of loose moderation on fedi is good for attention/growth (what many news fans want here), but bad for tight communities. getting that wrong hurts both.\",\"https://liberal.city/@wjmaggos/116969610165938479\",\"2026-07-23T13:50:08.000Z\",0,1,1\n  \"116969833093814576\",Tho99@mendeddrum.org,\"Thomas =:-)\",\"@wjmaggos we could have, but didn’t\",\"https://mendeddrum.org/@Tho99/116969833003554880\",\"2026-07-23T14:46:48.000Z\",3,0,0\nfetched_comment_count: 5\nprovider: Mastodon\nembed_ref: mastodon-it-s-ePc\napp_id: social_media\nskill_id: get-posts",
