        "type": "social_post",
        "content": "id: \"117043346514398510\"\nplatform: mastodon\npage: Mastodon@mastodon.social\ntitle: \"@Mastodon: We're excited to share the results from Mastodon's first #DiscoveryWeek! In case\"\nbody: \"We're excited to share the results from Mastodon's first #DiscoveryWeek!\\nIn case you missed it, earlier this year our Head of Design @imanijoy arranged a week of workshops and surveys to get to know you, learn about your needs and wants, and discover how you're using (and want to use) Mastodon.\\nThis week was tremendously helpful for us, and we're grateful to everyone who participated.\\nHere's what we learned:\\nhttps://blog.joinmastodon.org/2026/08/discovery-week-2026-what-we-learned-and-what-were-doing-next/\\n#Mastodon #Fediverse #SocialWeb #OpenSocial\"\nauthor: Mastodon\nauthor_display_name: Mastodon\nauthor_avatar_url: \"https://files.mastodon.social/accounts/avatars/000/013/179/original/b4ceb19c9c54ec7e.png\"\nurl: \"https://mastodon.social/@Mastodon/117043346514398510\"\npublished_at: \"2026-08-05T14:22:15.639Z\"\nreply_count: 12\nrepost_count: 159\nlike_count: 226\nmedia_url: null\nthumbnail_url: null\nexternal_url: \"https://blog.joinmastodon.org/2026/08/discovery-week-2026-what-we-learned-and-what-were-doing-next/\"\nexternal_title: \"Discovery Week 2026: What we learned, and what we’re doing next\"\ncomments[5]{id,author,author_display_name,body,url,published_at,like_count,reply_count,repost_count}:\n  \"117043482588002992\",chris@nutmeg.social,Chris Hayes,\"@Mastodon @imanijoy Great report. All good points. Very much agreed on boosting, threading, and hashtags.\\n“Survey respondents were asked about the\\ncircumstances in which they typically limit\\ntheir postsʼ visibility. The #1 reason\\nreported was to avoid spamming others\\nwhen replying.”\\nis interesting to see because 'Quiet Public' doesn't do that. (I used to make that mistake.)\\nFunny to read that others also have a list specifically for quieter posters. Mine is titled \\\"Never miss a post.\\\"\",\"https://nutmeg.social/@chris/117043480691144967\",\"2026-08-05T14:56:23.000Z\",3,1,0\n  \"117043975132435787\",clare_hooley@mastodon.me.uk,Clare Hooley,\"@chris it does to the extent it doesn’t show on local or federated feeds if you’re on a server with those (and I think also think in hashtags feeds if you have hashtags in it). Works out better for me for replies anyway; notify the person I’m replying to but doesn’t clutter local feed, but people can still see it if they want. Mind, I have turned replies off for my main feed and have done for a long time, so I tend to forget that’s not the default!\",\"https://mastodon.me.uk/@clare_hooley/117043974998912242\",\"2026-08-05T17:02:05.000Z\",1,0,0\n  \"117043651449867148\",lachralle@vivaldi.net,Ralf Demuth,@Mastodon @imanijoy Probably late to the game but please make all official apps and the web sites use the marker api to sync read states ceoss-platform.,\"https://social.vivaldi.net/@lachralle/117043650894046860\",\"2026-08-05T15:39:40.000Z\",1,0,0\n  \"117044569428922118\",antimundo@mastodon.gamedev.place,Antimundo,\"@Mastodon This post is honestly awesome, it's really cool to see something as simple as the team talking with the community. I really appreciate the work I've seen from you so far @imanijoy cheers!\",\"https://mastodon.gamedev.place/@antimundo/117044569400913047\",\"2026-08-05T19:33:15.000Z\",5,1,0\n  \"117044596654579027\",imanijoy,Imani,@antimundo thank you so much!,\"https://mastodon.social/@imanijoy/117044596654579027\",\"2026-08-05T19:40:11.263Z\",1,0,0\nfetched_comment_count: 5\nprovider: Mastodon\nembed_ref: mastodon-we-re-WKA\napp_id: social_media\nskill_id: get-posts",
